# Driver source packaged by packaging/build-deb.sh (sourced as shell, through
# packaging/version.sh, which also test-deb.sh and the release workflow use).
#
# The source is driver/upstream/: a byte-identical copy of UPSTREAM_COMMIT,
# checked against driver/upstream/SHA256SUMS at build time and against GitHub
# in CI. Our changes are the patch series driver/patches/ (driver/README.md).
#
# Version mapping (computed by packaging/version.sh):
#
#   FORK_VERSION FORK_RC  git tag         Debian version   DKMS PACKAGE_VERSION  MODULE_VERSION
#   (empty)      (empty)  v0.2.1-1        0.2.1-1          0.2.1                 0.2.0 (upstream, as is)
#   sr1          rc1      v0.2.1-sr1-rc1  0.2.1+sr1~rc1-1  0.2.1+sr1~rc1         0.2.1+sr1~rc1
#   sr1          (empty)  v0.2.1-sr1      0.2.1+sr1-1      0.2.1+sr1             0.2.1+sr1
#
# - FORK_VERSION empty = legacy scheme: unchanged upstream, driver/patches/series
#   must be empty, tag v<upstream>-<PKG_REV>. A packaging-only change: PKG_REV + 1.
# - FORK_VERSION srN = our downstream revision N on this upstream base ("sr" =
#   SirRenix). Every change (driver or packaging) is a new srN or rcN; PKG_REV
#   stays 1. FORK_RC rcN marks a pre-release (Debian "~" sorts it before the
#   final srN; the GitHub release is marked as pre-release).
# - Order is one-way: sr1~rc1 < sr1~rc2 < sr1 < sr2~rc1 < sr2. After a final
#   srN the next version is sr(N+1)[~rcM], never srN~rcM again (it would sort
#   below srN and apt would not upgrade).
# - With FORK_VERSION set, the patch series must make MODULE_VERSION equal the
#   DKMS PACKAGE_VERSION (patch 0001), so rc and final differ in modinfo;
#   build-deb.sh checks it.
# - A new upstream base: import it into driver/upstream/ (driver/README.md),
#   set UPSTREAM_TAG + UPSTREAM_COMMIT, PACKAGE_VERSION in deploy/dkms.conf to
#   the upstream version, FORK_VERSION back to sr1 (or empty without patches),
#   PKG_REV back to 1.
# - deploy/dkms.conf is the template: build-deb.sh writes PACKAGE_VERSION into
#   the packaged copy. Its own PACKAGE_VERSION stays the upstream version,
#   because deploy/install.sh (hand path, unpatched upstream clone) uses it.
UPSTREAM_REPO=https://github.com/ltdstudio/minisforum-n5-it5571.git
UPSTREAM_TAG=v0.2.1
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=feb6d9a5fbf6662a52fa7496009537945d2b30b0
PKG_REV=1
FORK_VERSION=sr1
FORK_RC=
